mapping "FPD96.1" source="FPD96" target="SNOMED_CT:429211003" relationship=source_is_broader_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        SE-mirror sctid
        429211003 = SNOMED CT 429211003, ACTIVE in RF2 20260701 (valid_end 2099-12-31, invalid_reason
        empty, rf2). Crosswalk-confirmed via sctid_to_athena_id.tdl (429211003->4181800). The procedure
        concept 429211003 is active, not only the
        history-of situation 429218009. A
        defensible active standard target exists, so the mapping carries no invalid_reason. Target definition: 429211003 = surgical creation
        of atrial lesion lines (cut-and-sew or ablation energy) to interrupt AF re-entry circuits. Why
        narrower / : the source is a residual that captures MORE than just the Maze procedure (also
        surgical PVI, concomitant AF ablation during other cardiac surgery, etc.); the Maze procedure is
        one specific operation within that residual bucket, so the target is more specific than the
        source = narrower. Confidence per the residual+narrower rubric (narrower maps silently add
        specificity the source did not assert; residual source = real doubt). | Mirror-only lookup,
        citation empty.
        """
}
flag "FPD96.1.label-check" kind=label-contradicts-comment assertion="kka-snomed-ct@2026.1/FPD96.1"
