mapping "FPH00.1" source="FPH00" target="SNOMED_CT:141171000146104" relationship=source_is_broader_than_target effect=omitted quality=40 {
    confidence 3 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
    comment "en" """
        SE-mirror sctid
        141171000146104 = SNOMED CT 141171000146104, ACTIVE in RF2 20260701 (valid_end 2099-12-31,
        invalid_reason empty, provenance rf2). A defensible active standard target
        exists, so the mapping carries no invalid_reason. Target definition: - percutaneous/transvenous
        lead extraction using a powered sheath. Why narrower / not exact: the source says which in
        Swedish cardiac-surgery usage covers BOTH pacemaker AND ICD lead systems; the target FSN
        specifies only and does not explicitly name ICD leads. The target is therefore slightly more
        specific than the source (does not assert ICD-scope), so mapping_type=narrower rather than
        exact_match, and confidence (high-ish but not because of the residual ICD-scope ambiguity and no
        independent crosswalk - sctid 141171000146104 is NOT in sctid_to_athena_id.tdl, so no Athena
        crosswalk confirms it). Alternate/related target considered: 73371000146109 - also ACTIVE in SE
        mirror, but FSN implies complexity grading not asserted by source, so 141171000146104 remains
        the primary. | No web research used; mirror-only lookup, citation empty.
        """
}
